  "description": "OPLIST_ADMISSIBILITY_GRAMMAR_PREREG.md / _RESULTS.md (the design this seed builds) + OPLIST_ADMISSIBILITY_GRAMMAR_SLICE1_RESULTS.md (the first slice: 52 SynthOp nodes + the two SortBy productions) + PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_GAMMA_BULK_TRANSCRIPTION_PREREG.md/_RESULTS.md (this rung: the bulk transcription of the remaining 12 op-list evidence-gate sites named by OPLIST_ADMISSIBILITY_GRAMMAR_RESULTS.md section 1.1's own 14-site table, plus the necessary 13th bare-scalar-fallback DEFAULT_OPS baseline production found while verifying parity -- see that RESULTS doc section 4). The op-list boolean gate ladder inside eval_synth_enumerate (runners/dsl/src/synth_enumerate.rs) is Gamma-shaped -- a real generated multi-production admissible-move SET, CLAUDE.md's own 'set of allowed moves' test, not a quantity that changes (no sd-loop residual here). This seed now carries 57 static SynthOp nodes (one per REAL current OP_TABLE entry, re-verified live against source -- the earlier '52' count is stale, 5 more ops landed since: IntersectAll, UnionAll, DictFromPairs, Mod, Sqrt) and 15 Productions -- the original 2 SortBy gates (has_dict_value, has_list_of_lists) plus 13 new productions covering site A (is_string_shaped -> DEFAULT_STR_OPS), site B (is_list_shaped -> DEFAULT_OPS u LIST_EXTRA_OPS), sites C/D/E (output_is_listlike -> TupleOf/Sort/[+has_string_value]Split), site F (output_is_setlike -> SET_DEFAULT_OPS), sites G/H (has_string_value/has_float_value on the bare-scalar fallback branch), site I (has_float_value on the list-shaped branch -> Round), a completion of the has_dict_value site (DictItems/Reverse -- SortBy was already shipped for this evidence), site L (has_repeated_list_element on the list-shaped branch -> IndexedMap), site N (output_is_bare_int -> ParseInt), and a 13th production for the bare-scalar-fallback DEFAULT_OPS baseline (needed for genuine parity on plain-arithmetic specs, not itself one of the named 14 sites -- see the RESULTS doc). Site K (has_repeated_list_element on the SAME bare-scalar branch) was found DEAD in current source (its guard can never be true when the code path that would consume it is reached) and is NOT ported -- see the RESULTS doc section 3. Every production nested inside the Rust ladder's 'else if spec_is_list_shaped' arm carries an explicit Not(output_is_setlike) conjunct -- REQUIRED, not decorative: a Set/FrozenSet-shaped output always ALSO satisfies is_list_shaped (Set/FrozenSet are is_listlike), and output_is_setlike is checked earlier in the if/else-if chain, so without this exclusion a list-shaped-branch production would wrongly admit ops for every Set-shaped spec in the corpus (tasks 232/473), not a rare edge case. Bucket admits (sites A, B, F, G, and the has_dict_value completion, plus the 13th) use a single production keyed by the Term algebra's own already-shipped `In` (member-of-a-literal-list) operator instead of one production per op -- In is already load-bearing this exact way in seeds/conversation_capability_route.json and siblings, so this is an established idiom, not a new mechanism; Production.tgt matches by node TYPE only (never attrs), so op-name specificity has to live in `where_` regardless of whether it's Eq or In. SynthSpecShape now carries an ELEVENTH flag, output_is_dictlike (domains/prog_synthesis.py:: _synth_spec_shape_flags), added ONLY so the bare-scalar-fallback production can correctly exclude the DICT_DEFAULT_OPS branch a later rung (GroupCount/DictMerge) inserted into the ladder's if/else-if chain -- DICT_DEFAULT_OPS's own two new ops (GroupCount, DictMerge) stay OUT of Gamma scope entirely, not one of the 14 named sites. As before, Gamma verdicts here are recorded facts only -- run_enumerate's real op-list construction is untouched, still driven entirely by the hand-written Rust ladder; zero MBPP task-id changes are expected from this rung.",
